From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cristian Papa <pcristian292@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 14:20:29 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 46/48] net: xpon: omci: count a Set of MIB data sync as
 before, and log it

"wrap the MIB data sync counter from 255 to 1" also made a Set of the
ONU data MIB data sync attribute keep the value the OLT wrote instead of
counting the Set. G.988 makes the attribute writable but does not say
clearly which of the two the OLT then expects, and the agent has always
counted it with an OLT that works and does not re-provision after a
Deactivate_ONU-ID. With that OLT the change could only be neutral or
harmful.

Go back to counting the Set on top of the agent's own sequence, as
before that commit, and log the written and resulting values, rate
limited, so that a trace shows whether the OLT uses the attribute. The
255 to 1 wrap stays.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 net/xpon/omci/agent.c | 18 +++++++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/net/xpon/omci/agent.c b/net/xpon/omci/agent.c
index 344a2dd..b98ce26 100644
--- a/net/xpon/omci/agent.c
+++ b/net/xpon/omci/agent.c
@@ -3982,14 +3982,22 @@ static u8 omci_agent_set_locked(struct omci_device *odev, u16 class_id,
 			goto rollback_processing;
 	}
 	/*
-	 * MIB data sync is writable: the OLT aligns its copy by setting it,
-	 * so keep the value it wrote instead of counting the Set on top.
+	 * MIB data sync is writable. Whether the ONU should then hold the
+	 * written value or count the Set on top of its own sequence is not
+	 * settled, and the agent has always done the latter with an OLT that
+	 * works: keep that, and log what the OLT wrote so a trace can tell.
 	 */
 	if (class_id == OMCI_CLASS_ONU_DATA && !entity_id &&
-	    (apply & OMCI_ONU_DATA_MIB_SYNC_MASK))
-		omci_agent_set_mib_sync_locked(agent, object->data[0]);
-	else
+	    (apply & OMCI_ONU_DATA_MIB_SYNC_MASK)) {
+		u8 written = object->data[0];
+
 		omci_agent_increment_mib_sync_locked(agent);
+		dev_info_ratelimited(odev->parent,
+				     "OMCI: OLT set MIB data sync to %u, now %u\n",
+				     written, agent->mib_sync);
+	} else {
+		omci_agent_increment_mib_sync_locked(agent);
+	}
 	ret = OMCI_RESULT_SUCCESS;
 	goto out_free_previous;
 
